        "identity": {
          "graphId": "properties-and-authoring-contract",
          "nodeId": "properties-and-authoring-contract-goal"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/goal.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "body": "A node, an edge, a handle and a graph each has a panel built from one contract, so a switch is described once and every reader (the panel, a template, an agent) reads the same description.",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "successMetrics": [
          "The contract covers node, edge, handle and graph switches, each with where it is written, its default, its valid values and where it applies.",
          "Every switch has a control, or a stated reason it does not.",
          "Advanced is a last resort, not the way to set a switch.",
          "The old type tables, legacy payload keys and per-browser style presets are gone.",
          "The Properties panel is no longer one 6,200-line component."
        ],
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792950744123,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-27: the panels are built and light, and what is left is small. Node, edge, handle and graph panels read one contract (79 switches, schema v1); the old Document Properties dialog is History and GitHub in the browser's Document menu and its properties are in the graph panel; the preset styles, the Meaning section, the dialog's leftovers and the placeholder share data are gone; the layout section is grouped and closed; the default handle has a field; every primitive page shows its parts while browsing. Open: the Graph boundary review, splitting PropertiesPanel.js, the old tables and keys, and the canon page for the contract (wording to Michael first). Waiting on Michael: publish canon and redeploy the app. 2026-10-27, later: auditing the code against the contract turned up enough work to be a graph of its own (tasks/authoring-contract-enforcement); the task and portal at the foot of this graph open it. 2026-10-27, later: six switches nothing read were removed (autoSave, curveBias, edge flow, direction, strength, intent), so the contract is 79."
      }
