        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "The Properties panel is the schema's first consumer. A generic field per value type (boolean, number, enum, reference, rectangle) writing at the switch's write path. Start with the nine switches that have no control.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792950744125,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-26: built and seen. utils/contractFields.js (pure, tested), components/ContractFields.js, a Presentation section on the node panel (the switches for the selected kind that have no hand-built control), and an edge version under Line, More. Visible's hand-built toggle is retired; the rest follow only when a control is worth moving. semanticZoom.resolution and renderShape stay as they are (set by resizing the node, not by this panel). A smoke test writes every field through the editor's real updateNode and updateEdge and clears it again."
      }
