        "title": "Are the four selections the right separation: node, edge, handle, graph?",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "properties-and-authoring-contract",
          "nodeId": "properties-and-authoring-contract-q-selections"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/open-question.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "answered",
        "body": "Each gets its own panel, built from the same contract, with a scope value each. The graph panel would be the one with none today.\n\nDecision: Keep four authoring scopes: node, edge, handle, graph. These are distinct editing responsibilities, not necessarily four unrelated object kinds. Generate the appropriate panel from the shared authoring contract.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
