        "title": "Handle properties: right-click a handle",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "properties-and-authoring-contract",
          "nodeId": "properties-and-authoring-contract-handle-select"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "Decided, and refined by Michael: a handle is selectable on the canvas, and right-clicking it opens its properties. Dragging still starts a connection, so a right-click never competes with a drag. A Handle is a visual anchor, not the Port it references, and the parent node stays visible.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792986466258,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-26: decided not to build. Handle properties stay on the node panel, in the Handles section (collapsed rows, Placement and Port groups, one-connection toggle). No right-click on the canvas."
      }
    },
