      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Edges flicker when zooming",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "properties-and-authoring-contract",
          "nodeId": "properties-and-authoring-contract-edge-zoom-flicker"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "Found by recording the screen and reading it frame by frame. Two causes. Zooming out, edges that reached in from beyond the screen were missing until the gesture ended, because the edge canvas was exactly screen-sized: it now draws 600 px past every side (b6f84bb4). At the end of a zoom, the layers dropped the gesture's scale in the same render that moved the nodes, but the edges are redrawn after it, so every edge snapped back to its old position for one frame: the edge canvas now keeps the scale until EdgeLayer has drawn (f3a4a2dc). Michael checked the second video: the flicker is gone. An earlier attempt that drew the edges before paint read stale handle positions and made it worse; reverted.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793132273516,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-27: Found by recording the screen and reading it frame by frame."
      }
    },
